title: Start
---

Rain taps softly against the window.
A cramped studio apartment. Bills scattered across a small table. The room is dim except for the light of a phone screen.
The Player stares at the screen. 
<<play_animation Player Black>>

Player: …Rent… electricity… overdue notice?

The Player exhales.

Player: I can’t keep stretching it like this.

Her stomach growls. 

Player: …I really need a job. Anything at this point.

She goes to job search site and scrolls through job listings.

Part-time Café Staff – Experience required
Convenience Store Night Shift – Minimum wage
Warehouse Sorting – Heavy lifting required

Player: Minimum wage… heavy lifting… I won’t survive on that.

She scrolls further down.
The scrolling slows.

Private Residence | High Pay – Paid Immediately After Completion, No Experience Required

Player: ... One week?

She taps the listing.

- Clean designated areas only
- Do not enter restricted rooms
- Follow all instructions strictly
- Live-out position
- Generous compensation
A phone number is listed below. No company name. No address.

Player: ... Private residence?

She frowns.

Player: No company name… no photos… no reviews…

She scrolls. Nothing more.

Player: That's suspicious. But...

She breathes in.

Player: The pay. 

She rereads the number.

Player: That’s more than I'd make in a month.

The rain outside grows slightly louder.

What should I do?

-> Ignore it.
    Player: It’s probably some scam.
    Player: ... Or even worse. 
    A small pause.
    Player: ... But what if it isn't?
    She glances back at the unpaid bills.
    Player: I just need one week.
    <<jump PhoneCall>>
-> Call now.
    <<jump PhoneCall>>

===
title: PhoneCall
---
<<play_animation Player Grey>>

The phone rings once. 
Twice.

Click.

Land Lady: Hello?

Her voice is steady. Almost too steady.

Player: Ah, he- hello. I'm calling you about the cleaning job...

A brief pause.

Land Lady: A-ha. You saw the listing. 

Player: Yes... 

Land Lady: Can you start tomorrow morning? 8:00 AM sharp.

Player: Tomorrow morning? Ah, yes! I can do that.

Land Lady: Good. I need someone who follows directions and works without causing any trouble. Do you understand?

Player: Y-yes, of course. I won't cause any trouble.

Land Lady: The address is 104 Blackwood Lane. Don't be late.

Click.

Player: ...Hello? She hung up.

Player: 104 Blackwood Lane... Am I really going to be okay with this job?

Player: ...I should look around my room and then get some sleep for tomorrow.

<<set $has_finished_phone_call = true>>
===

title: Mansion_Entrance_Arrival
---
Player: So this is the house... 

Player: It's much bigger and darker than I imagined.

Player: Well, no turning back now... Let's go knock on the door.
===

title: First_Talk

---



*press E on the mansion door, cutscene start without asking (controls locked)*

Before you try to knock on the door, the door opens by itself.



Alice: ...! He-Hello.



Butler: You arrived just on time. Come on in.



*Both move into the mansion*
<<teleport_with_delay LivingRoom_Transition 2.0>>


Butler: This is our living room. You will be working upstairs.

Butler: The first room you see when you get up there.



*camera moves up to the 2nd floor hallway, and comes back*



Butler: This is your room here. Rest today, and your work will start from tomorrow.

Butler: And wear these while you stay here.



*butler turns around to alice, hands the uniform*



Butler: ... You can do anything you like, but just one rule you must follow.

Butler: Stay inside your room late at night. Do not wander around after hours.



Butler: As for today, you are free to rest and look around the mansion. Just make sure not to cause any trouble.

Butler: I will see you tomorrow morning.

Alice: Ah, thank...



*The Butler leaves*



Alice: ... She just left. 



*Alice steps inside her assigned room*
<<teleport_with_delay Bedroom_Transition 1.0>>



Alice: Wow... it's really old and small.

Alice: Well, at least it has a bed...

Alice: Before I look around the mansion, I should change into the maid uniform first.



<<change_clothes Maid>>



Alice: Alright, everything fits. Time to explore.

===

title: Normal_Ending
---
(The sun rises on Day {$day_count}. You've completed your 3 days of work at the mansion...)

Alice: My time here is done. Let's get changed first...

<<change_clothes Modern>>
===

title: Normal_Ending_Cutscene
---
// This runs as soon as Alice steps on the trigger box outside the Bedroom on Day4
Alice: !
Butler: Good morning.
Alice: Ah, good mor-
Butler: You have done a great job for last three days.
Butler: Money is sent through your bank accound this morning.
Alice: Oh, thank... thank you. 
Alice: 'That was very quick...'
Butler: You may leave as soon as you pack up.
-> Alice: Can I say good byes to other people before I leave?
    Butler: No, I need you to leave ASAP. 
    Alice: 'She's in such a hurry...'
    Alice: O, okay.
    Butler: I'll walk you to the door. 
-> Alice: I think I'm ready to leave.
    Butler: Great. I'll walk you to the door. 

<<teleport_with_delay Exit_Transition 2.5>>

Alice: ...
Alice: That felt like a dream...
Alice: ...
Alice: ......
Alice: Let's go home. 

===
title: Normal_Ending_Credit
---

Normal Ending Finished.
===